          "fields": {
            "key": "NEXT_TRACK",
            "state": "press",
            "sender": "IrRemote"
          }
        },
        "logs": []
      },
      "divergence": "DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE from the pre-rebuild code, 2026-09-22, when the twelve regex and scanner reads of speaker XML became one bounded parser (OPEN-WORK 133). Same cause as the observer corpus's case of this name: the old state and sender patterns spelled the value in double quotes, so a well-formed single-quoted element lost both. The parser reads them. Nothing a recorded speaker sent is affected."
    },
    {
      "name": "key_press: two keyData elements",
      "input": {
        "op": "key_press",
        "body": "<keyData state=\"press\">NEXT_TRACK</keyData><keyData state=\"release\">PREV_TRACK</keyData>"
      },
      "expect": {
        "value": null,
        "logs": []
      },
      "divergence": "DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE from the pre-rebuild code, 2026-09-22, when the twelve regex and scanner reads of speaker XML became one bounded parser (OPEN-WORK 133). This body has TWO root elements, so it is not a well-formed XML document at all, and the parser refuses it whole rather than reading the first element out of it. The old scanner took the first. A speaker has never sent this; what the case pins now is that an unparseable body is answered as no key press, which is how every other unreadable body is answered."
    },
