    {
      "name": "key_press: markup inside the key",
      "input": {
        "op": "key_press",
        "body": "<keyData state=\"press\"><b>NEXT</b></keyData>"
      },
      "expect": {
        "value": {
          "type": "KeyPress",
          "fields": {
            "key": "",
            "state": "press",
            "sender": ""
          }
        },
        "logs": []
      },
      "divergence": "DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE from the pre-rebuild code, 2026-09-22, when the twelve regex and scanner reads of speaker XML became one bounded parser (OPEN-WORK 133). The old scanner returned the raw inner text of the element, markup included, so the key came back as the string <b>NEXT</b>. A key is a token a speaker names, never a document, so the parser reads the element's TEXT and nested markup is not part of it - which leaves the key empty here. The press is still reported, exactly as an empty keyData was before."
    },
